# Domain Layer Standards

The domain layer has ZERO dependencies on Flutter, Drift, Riverpod, or any external package.

**PERMITTED:** `dart:core`, `equatable`, `freezed_annotation`, `fpdart`
**FORBIDDEN:** `package:flutter/*`, `package:drift/*`, `package:riverpod/*`, `package:dio/*`, `lib/data/`, `lib/presentation/`

## Entities — Freezed Immutable Data Classes

- Use `@freezed` annotation. All fields use named parameters.
- Domain entities do NOT have `toJson()` — serialization is the data layer's job.
- Use `copyWith()` for modifications. Collections are unmodifiable views.
- Every mutable entity MUST include: `id` (String, UUID v4), `createdAt`, `updatedAt`, `isDeleted` (default false), `syncVersion` (default 0).

```dart
@freezed
class Ledger with _$Ledger {
  const factory Ledger({
    required String id,
    required String name,
    required LedgerType type,
    required String icon,
    required String color,
    required int sortOrder,
    required DateTime createdAt,
    required DateTime updatedAt,
    @Default(false) bool isDeleted,
    @Default(0) int syncVersion,
  }) = _Ledger;
}
```

## Value Objects — Self-Validating Types

- `Money`: amount as `int` + `currencyCode`. Arithmetic ops, display formatting via `Currency.decimalPlaces`.
- `PhoneNumber`: validation, normalization, WhatsApp deep-link generation.
- Immutable. Factory constructors validate on creation. Invalid state is unrepresentable.

## Repository Interfaces

- Abstract classes in `lib/domain/repositories/`.
- Return `Either<Failure, T>` for fallible operations. `Stream` for reactive queries.
- Cohesive — split by aggregate root. No God repositories.
- Document behavioral contracts in dartdoc.

## Failure Hierarchy — Sealed Error Types

```dart
sealed class Failure {
  final String message;
  final String? code;
  const Failure(this.message, {this.code});
}
final class DatabaseFailure extends Failure { ... }
final class ValidationFailure extends Failure { ... }
final class NetworkFailure extends Failure { ... }
final class StorageFailure extends Failure { ... }
final class AuthFailure extends Failure { ... }
final class LimitExceededFailure extends Failure {
  final String featureKey;
  final int currentCount;
  final int maxAllowed;
}
```

## Enums

- `LedgerType`: customers, suppliers, personal, custom
- `TransactionType`: debt, payment
- `BackupType`: local, cloud
- PascalCase type, camelCase values. Exhaustive `switch` expressions.

## Dartdoc

All public APIs MUST have `///` dartdoc. Document business meaning of each field, validation rules, behavioral contracts.
